# Least-privilege sudoers rule for the DeadDrop app's own runtime needs.
#
# The deployed server/client binaries run as the unprivileged `connor`
# user (see deaddrop-alpha.service/deaddrop-bravo.service's
# User=/Group=), and the ONLY reason they ever need root at all is
# NetworkManager's polkit rules requiring elevated privileges to add
# a new WiFi connection profile or force a fresh scan (see wifi.c's
# own comments - activating an ALREADY-KNOWN profile doesn't need
# this, only these two specific operations do).
#
# This file exists to make that real: even if the much broader
# 010-connor-nopasswd rule (unscoped, ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD:ALL - see its
# own file, and TESTING.md's 2026-08-23 security audit entry for the
# tradeoff reasoning) were ever narrowed or removed, the app's actual
# runtime functionality (the Ctrl+W WiFi setup screen) keeps working
# unattended with exactly this and nothing more.
#
# Install as /etc/sudoers.d/020-deaddrop-wifi (mode 440, root:root -
# same as every other file in this directory; sudo refuses to read a
# sudoers.d file with unsafe permissions).
Cmnd_Alias DEADDROP_WIFI = /usr/bin/nmcli device wifi rescan, /usr/bin/nmcli device wifi connect *
connor ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: DEADDROP_WIFI
